SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The eerrrr() and wwaarrnn() families of functions are BSD extensions.  As such
     they should not be used in truly portable code.  Use ssttrreerrrroorr() or simi‐
     lar functions instead.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The eerrrr() and wwaarrnn() functions first appeared in 4.4BSD.  The
     eerrrr__sseett__eexxiitt() and eerrrr__sseett__ffiillee() functions first appeared in
     FreeBSD 2.1.  The eerrrrcc() and wwaarrnncc() functions first appeared in
     FreeBSD 3.0.

